.TH HTTP_DUMP 3
.SH NAME
http_dump \- print the state of an HTTP client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "void http_dump(http* " h ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_dump ()
writes one line to standard error with the socket, the flags that are set, the last error and the state of the
response (status code, transfer, byte counts, the first 100 bytes of the headers).
It is a debugging aid; the library has to be built with DEBUG_HTTP defined, otherwise the
function does nothing.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_request_dump(3), http_response_dump(3)
